    "description": "- Architect and develop a planet-scale simulation game combining procedural generation, applied mathematics, and data-driven gameplay systems.\n- Design a multiscale world architecture connecting a spherical planetary simulation with detailed local sites while preserving geographic consistency across terrain, climate, biomes, rivers, urbanization, and environmental conditions.\n- Design a deterministic, component-based simulation architecture for entities and physical processes, using double buffering and extensible systems to support complex interactions.\n- Build environmental systems for fluid flow, thermal diffusion, contamination, and reactions across local maps containing up to 180,224 tiles, distributing computational work across simulation ticks to maintain responsive performance.\n- Own the complete technical lifecycle, including system design, implementation, debugging, performance optimization, development tooling, extensibility, and long-term architectural planning.",
